Let LLVM's Windows support code run on Windows XP.

Vista and Windows 7 APIs that LLVM (and lldb, see 0002) call directly are
replaced by the XPCompat.h stand-ins, which use the real function when the
system has it and an XP fallback otherwise.  Calls that pass Windows 7
flags to older functions (FindFirstFileExW, LoadLibraryExA) are retried
without them.  PSAPI_VERSION 1 takes the process status functions from
psapi.dll.

